1
00:00:09,550 --> 00:00:10,250
Damn it.

2
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:13,480
I can't sleep at all.

3
00:00:16,079 --> 00:00:18,410
Ah!

4
00:00:21,460 --> 00:00:22,300
What on earth

5
00:00:23,390 --> 00:00:26,160
is wrong with me?

6
00:00:31,090 --> 00:00:33,460
Wait, am I the bottom?

7
00:00:34,160 --> 00:00:35,060
Well...

8
00:00:37,510 --> 00:00:38,900
What the hell are you laughing at?

9
00:00:38,900 --> 00:00:40,180
This is too weird.

10
00:00:55,720 --> 00:00:57,420
You like me, don't you?

11
00:01:02,950 --> 00:01:04,040
Probably.

12
00:01:05,340 --> 00:01:07,370
It's all his fault.

13
00:01:09,120 --> 00:01:10,010
He clearly

14
00:01:10,970 --> 00:01:12,560
did that to me.

15
00:01:13,880 --> 00:01:21,310
[Exchange Student Recruitment]

16
00:01:31,180 --> 00:01:32,130
Here you go.

17
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:38,650
Change your clothes and come out quickly.

18
00:01:38,650 --> 00:01:40,880
We need to thank Kana and Nanami.

19
00:01:41,380 --> 00:01:44,270
He's acting like nothing ever happened.

20
00:01:42,630 --> 00:01:44,420
[Campus Open Day]

21
00:01:44,310 --> 00:01:45,670
Just like usual.

22
00:01:48,900 --> 00:01:52,680
But well, he's so handsome,
no wonder you can't let it go.

23
00:01:52,700 --> 00:01:53,560
But to him,

24
00:01:53,580 --> 00:01:57,060
it might just be like
getting a mosquito bite.

25
00:01:57,950 --> 00:02:00,250
Ah!

26
00:02:01,310 --> 00:02:01,950
Hey.

27
00:02:01,970 --> 00:02:03,750
I know very well
that even if two people do that,

28
00:02:03,750 --> 00:02:06,420
it doesn't mean
they have to be in a relationship.

29
00:02:06,420 --> 00:02:08,310
Besides, I like girls.

30
00:02:08,440 --> 00:02:10,949
I don't know much about Issei's situation,

31
00:02:11,790 --> 00:02:13,770
but with his conditions,

32
00:02:13,900 --> 00:02:16,829
he can find as many as he wants,
regardless of gender.

33
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:20,590
I know.

34
00:02:21,130 --> 00:02:24,480
I know better than anyone, but...

35
00:02:27,590 --> 00:02:30,570
Why did he say "probably"?

36
00:02:30,600 --> 00:02:33,040
Ah!

37
00:02:54,160 --> 00:02:56,660
♪ Through the crack in the window ♪

38
00:02:56,680 --> 00:03:00,570
♪ Summer sunlight streams on down ♪

39
00:03:00,600 --> 00:03:04,860
♪ OH YEAH, beneath the endless blue sky ♪

40
00:03:04,880 --> 00:03:08,220
♪ I make a promise deep inside, YEAH ♪

41
00:03:08,250 --> 00:03:10,660
♪ From today on,
I'll fill the pages with my thoughts ♪

42
00:03:10,680 --> 00:03:12,640
♪ Along with all those silly words ♪

43
00:03:12,660 --> 00:03:15,930
♪ I'm just one step away from you ♪

44
00:03:15,950 --> 00:03:18,329
♪ One little leap is all it takes ♪

45
00:03:18,360 --> 00:03:20,320
♪ Before the summer comes to an end ♪

46
00:03:20,320 --> 00:03:23,750
♪ I'll leave my mark on your heart ♪

47
00:03:23,780 --> 00:03:25,860
♪ 'Cause I feel the breeze ♪

48
00:03:25,880 --> 00:03:27,780
♪ Only this moment matters ♪

49
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:31,100
♪ I make a wish upon the heavens ♪

50
00:03:31,120 --> 00:03:34,430
♪ OK, as for tomorrow ♪

51
00:03:34,450 --> 00:03:39,220
♪ Let tomorrow's wind take care of it ♪

52
00:03:39,250 --> 00:03:43,020
♪ YEAH, open up this door ♪

53
00:03:43,040 --> 00:03:46,940
♪ And let's set off together ♪

54
00:03:46,970 --> 00:03:49,930
♪ Summer vibe, no tomorrow, summer vibe ♪

55
00:03:49,950 --> 00:03:54,750
♪ This one-of-a-kind view ♪

56
00:03:54,770 --> 00:03:58,490
♪ This feeling of breaking free ♪

57
00:03:58,510 --> 00:04:02,220
♪ Nothing can stand in our way ♪

58
00:04:02,240 --> 00:04:03,900
♪ Summer vibe ♪

59
00:04:03,920 --> 00:04:05,510
♪ Summer vibe ♪

60
00:04:05,540 --> 00:04:08,470
♪ In the clear summer sky ♪

61
00:04:08,280 --> 00:04:11,060
[It's Just Business Episode 3]

62
00:04:08,500 --> 00:04:11,250
♪ Drifting all around, summer vibe ♪

63
00:04:19,200 --> 00:04:19,959
Ren.

64
00:04:19,980 --> 00:04:21,420
Good morning.

65
00:04:21,440 --> 00:04:24,690
-Good morning.
-Aren't they the legendary two?

66
00:04:24,710 --> 00:04:27,470
-Morning.
-So handsome. Like a painting.

67
00:04:27,500 --> 00:04:28,620
Good morning.

68
00:04:28,640 --> 00:04:30,800
He's still putting on the same act
as always,

69
00:04:30,800 --> 00:04:33,800
with a cold expression
as if nothing happened before.

70
00:04:36,580 --> 00:04:39,180
What does this guy want?

71
00:04:47,640 --> 00:04:49,150
Ah, they are here.

72
00:04:50,510 --> 00:04:52,010
That flashy hair.

73
00:04:53,700 --> 00:04:55,090
Ren.

74
00:04:56,380 --> 00:04:58,570
Here, this is your top from before.

75
00:04:58,590 --> 00:04:59,780
It's already washed.

76
00:04:59,780 --> 00:05:02,120
Thank you, you really helped me a lot.

77
00:05:02,380 --> 00:05:04,430
Ren is such a clumsy guy.

78
00:05:08,370 --> 00:05:10,700
He doesn't understand my feelings at all.

79
00:05:11,790 --> 00:05:12,950
But I was really startled at the time.

80
00:05:12,950 --> 00:05:15,000
I can't believe someone could make
such a loud noise dropping tableware.

81
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:16,700
It's the first time I've seen that
since I started college.

82
00:05:16,700 --> 00:05:17,960
I'm really sorry.

83
00:05:19,690 --> 00:05:22,010
Ren, are you a little tired?

84
00:05:23,090 --> 00:05:26,050
You look a bit off today, and you've got
dark circles under your eyes.

85
00:05:26,050 --> 00:05:26,720
Really?

86
00:05:27,330 --> 00:05:29,070
Ah, sorry. I shouldn't have said that.

87
00:05:29,070 --> 00:05:30,380
Ah, no, it's fine.

88
00:05:33,220 --> 00:05:34,950
Couldn't you sleep last night?

89
00:05:36,300 --> 00:05:37,310
No, not really.

90
00:05:38,300 --> 00:05:41,760
Ah, maybe I've just been too busy
with my part-time job lately.

91
00:05:42,940 --> 00:05:43,900
If you have any troubles,
just come talk to me.

92
00:05:43,900 --> 00:05:44,860
About anything.

93
00:05:45,210 --> 00:05:47,450
I'll definitely do my best to help you.

94
00:05:47,470 --> 00:05:48,800
Thank you.

95
00:05:49,750 --> 00:05:50,450
But,

96
00:05:50,800 --> 00:05:51,930
Ren, you already have

97
00:05:51,930 --> 00:05:54,890
Issei by you side.
My concern might be unnecessary.

98
00:05:56,090 --> 00:05:58,680
Ah, how should I put this?

99
00:06:05,950 --> 00:06:08,540
Actually, this guy
is the source of all my worries.

100
00:06:08,540 --> 00:06:09,730
But I can't say it.

101
00:06:13,730 --> 00:06:16,430
Ah, right, I need to thank you two.

102
00:06:16,460 --> 00:06:17,340
-Eh?
-Eh?

103
00:06:17,950 --> 00:06:20,950
You washed my clothes
and helped me find a shower room.

104
00:06:21,530 --> 00:06:23,260
Is there anything you two want?

105
00:06:25,950 --> 00:06:29,110
Um, if you two are okay with it,

106
00:06:29,130 --> 00:06:32,260
how about the four of us
hang out together on Sunday?

107
00:06:34,070 --> 00:06:35,500
Not like a date,

108
00:06:35,520 --> 00:06:38,120
just good friends hanging out.

109
00:06:38,830 --> 00:06:43,070
Um, well...

110
00:06:43,270 --> 00:06:45,190
Sounds good. Let's go.

111
00:06:45,720 --> 00:06:46,390
Eh?

112
00:06:46,420 --> 00:06:48,100
Great.

113
00:06:48,120 --> 00:06:49,980
Then let's get in touch later.

114
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:51,530
We still have class,

115
00:06:51,990 --> 00:06:53,050
so we'll get going.

116
00:06:53,060 --> 00:06:54,570
Bye.

117
00:07:03,850 --> 00:07:04,810
Are we going?

118
00:07:07,890 --> 00:07:09,870
Don't you want to go?

119
00:07:11,940 --> 00:07:14,070
No, I do want to go.

120
00:07:15,700 --> 00:07:16,700
Then that's fine.

121
00:07:18,960 --> 00:07:19,640
No.

122
00:07:20,700 --> 00:07:22,270
It's not a bad thing anyway.

123
00:07:29,840 --> 00:07:31,610
This kind of four-person date,

124
00:07:32,170 --> 00:07:34,120
at first, the four of us
will have fun together.

125
00:07:34,120 --> 00:07:35,550
Then it'll naturally split into two pairs,

126
00:07:35,550 --> 00:07:37,880
and each pair can develop
their own chemistry.

127
00:07:37,880 --> 00:07:41,080
Finally, we'll disband
and go our separate ways in pairs.

128
00:07:46,159 --> 00:07:48,560
How about the four of us
hang out together?

129
00:07:49,420 --> 00:07:51,300
Sounds good. Let's go.

130
00:07:51,320 --> 00:07:52,070
Eh?

131
00:07:54,659 --> 00:07:56,940
You like me, don't you?

132
00:07:58,510 --> 00:07:59,930
Probably.

133
00:08:04,230 --> 00:08:06,090
What exactly is that guy thinking

134
00:08:07,980 --> 00:08:10,760
about his relationship with me?

135
00:08:13,040 --> 00:08:15,070
So annoying.

136
00:08:26,920 --> 00:08:27,950
So sleepy.

137
00:08:33,330 --> 00:08:34,690
Are you okay?

138
00:08:34,990 --> 00:08:35,570
Eh?

139
00:08:35,590 --> 00:08:38,950
It's finally Sunday,
and you're looking all gloomy.

140
00:08:38,970 --> 00:08:41,179
What's wrong? What happened?
Did you get dumped?

141
00:08:41,179 --> 00:08:42,150
No, I didn't.

142
00:08:42,179 --> 00:08:43,980
Then stop pulling such a sour face.

143
00:08:43,980 --> 00:08:46,740
Being with you
is going to bring me bad luck too.

144
00:08:46,760 --> 00:08:47,890
You're so annoying.

145
00:08:49,680 --> 00:08:51,610
Hey, sis, are you going out?

146
00:08:51,630 --> 00:08:52,970
Yeah. That obvious?

147
00:08:53,980 --> 00:08:58,120
A date. With someone I met recently.

148
00:09:00,130 --> 00:09:01,260
Hope you get dumped.

149
00:09:02,340 --> 00:09:05,390
Idiot! Bye.

150
00:09:11,980 --> 00:09:13,010
That's true.

151
00:09:14,620 --> 00:09:15,870
I'm going on a date.

152
00:09:16,230 --> 00:09:18,530
I should stop thinking
about all that nonsense.

153
00:09:18,530 --> 00:09:21,160
Just enjoy myself.

154
00:09:21,530 --> 00:09:22,640
Anyway,

155
00:09:23,090 --> 00:09:26,610
I like girls. I'm so sleepy.

156
00:09:26,640 --> 00:09:28,790
What should we do today?

157
00:09:28,820 --> 00:09:29,360
Take purikura?

158
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:30,770
-Right? I thought purikura would be good too.
-Yeah.

159
00:09:30,770 --> 00:09:31,770
-I want to take purikura.
-Yeah. And after that?

160
00:09:31,770 --> 00:09:33,040
After taking purikura...

161
00:09:33,040 --> 00:09:34,110
-Sorry to keep you waiting.
-we could go bowling.

162
00:09:34,110 --> 00:09:35,460
Yeah... Issei.

163
00:09:35,890 --> 00:09:36,980
What are these?

164
00:09:37,010 --> 00:09:38,540
They're cinnamon rolls.

165
00:09:38,540 --> 00:09:39,590
We arrived a little early,

166
00:09:39,590 --> 00:09:41,950
-so I went to buy this with Nanami.
-Yeah.

167
00:09:43,820 --> 00:09:45,380
Oh, thank you.

168
00:09:46,050 --> 00:09:47,840
It looks delicious, right?

169
00:09:47,870 --> 00:09:48,270
Yeah.

170
00:09:48,290 --> 00:09:49,630
Really?

171
00:10:05,080 --> 00:10:05,980
That's true.

172
00:10:07,620 --> 00:10:10,780
Issei has always been good
at getting along with girls.

173
00:10:11,490 --> 00:10:14,310
Looks like Kana and Issei
are a pair today.

174
00:10:14,340 --> 00:10:15,390
And then?

175
00:10:15,410 --> 00:10:16,500
Ren!

176
00:10:17,970 --> 00:10:18,560
Ah.

177
00:10:21,090 --> 00:10:22,710
Sorry, I'm late.

178
00:10:24,230 --> 00:10:25,300
Here you go.

179
00:10:25,320 --> 00:10:25,920
Yeah.

180
00:10:26,250 --> 00:10:27,980
Thank you. It looks delicious.

181
00:10:27,980 --> 00:10:30,290
We're going to be playing for a while,
so we need to fuel up first.

182
00:10:30,290 --> 00:10:32,520
Nanami and I are a pair.

183
00:10:36,620 --> 00:10:37,790
Are you okay?

184
00:10:39,390 --> 00:10:40,230
What's wrong?

185
00:10:42,080 --> 00:10:44,240
So where are we going? This way?

186
00:10:44,270 --> 00:10:45,270
-Let's go.
-Okay.

187
00:10:45,880 --> 00:10:47,110
Alright.

188
00:10:47,130 --> 00:10:47,930
What are you spacing out for?

189
00:10:47,930 --> 00:10:49,650
Eh? Bowling?

190
00:10:49,670 --> 00:10:50,700
Bowling?

191
00:11:01,390 --> 00:11:03,020
Oh, boo-hoo.

192
00:11:03,040 --> 00:11:04,130
-What a pity!
-What a pity!

193
00:11:04,130 --> 00:11:05,370
Don't mind.

194
00:11:05,390 --> 00:11:07,210
-Don't mind. Don't mind.
-Heave-ho.

195
00:11:07,210 --> 00:11:08,430
Issei, we're counting on you.

196
00:11:08,430 --> 00:11:09,500
Thanks.

197
00:11:19,040 --> 00:11:20,230
So handsome.

198
00:11:20,260 --> 00:11:22,810
Wow, Issei is amazing!

199
00:11:22,840 --> 00:11:23,700
Not bad at all.

200
00:11:23,720 --> 00:11:25,810
That's awesome!

201
00:11:30,980 --> 00:11:33,060
So pleasing to the eye. Like a star.

202
00:11:33,090 --> 00:11:35,620
It's not good to keep staring at him
like that.

203
00:11:36,290 --> 00:11:37,080
Look.

204
00:11:37,100 --> 00:11:39,380
As expected of Issei.

205
00:11:40,480 --> 00:11:41,480
Just average.

206
00:11:41,510 --> 00:11:42,290
Oh my.

207
00:11:42,310 --> 00:11:44,620
Why are you getting so smug too, Ren?

208
00:11:46,940 --> 00:11:48,380
But that's the truth.

209
00:11:49,700 --> 00:11:52,860
[Kanako] [Issei] [Ren] [Nanami]

210
00:11:58,040 --> 00:11:59,350
That's amazing!

211
00:11:59,380 --> 00:12:01,430
Oh my.

212
00:12:02,200 --> 00:12:03,730
But this one was too easy.

213
00:12:03,750 --> 00:12:04,620
Easy?

214
00:12:05,550 --> 00:12:06,980
It's not easy at all.

215
00:12:07,520 --> 00:12:08,380
Ren.

216
00:12:09,090 --> 00:12:10,770
We have to do our best too.

217
00:12:12,760 --> 00:12:14,520
Ah, yeah.

218
00:12:14,620 --> 00:12:15,270
Yeah.

219
00:12:15,290 --> 00:12:16,280
That's right!

220
00:12:16,310 --> 00:12:17,580
-Go for it!
-Go for it!

221
00:12:17,600 --> 00:12:18,520
Here I come!

222
00:12:18,540 --> 00:12:19,490
Charge!

223
00:12:19,520 --> 00:12:20,520
I'll get a strike.

224
00:12:21,110 --> 00:12:23,320
Phew.

225
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:24,770
Get a strike.

226
00:12:24,800 --> 00:12:25,770
Alright.

227
00:12:25,800 --> 00:12:27,770
Charge!

228
00:12:29,920 --> 00:12:31,050
Go for it!

229
00:12:45,080 --> 00:12:47,090
Ah, me? Well...

230
00:12:47,860 --> 00:12:51,490
Ah, I'm not in good shape!
Why is this happening?

231
00:12:51,520 --> 00:12:54,590
Ah, I think I sprained my wrist! It hurts!

232
00:12:55,100 --> 00:12:56,130
Ah, a sprain.

233
00:12:56,160 --> 00:12:57,920
It shouldn't hurt that much, right?

234
00:12:57,920 --> 00:12:59,100
It hurts so much!

235
00:12:59,130 --> 00:13:02,550
Oh, Ren, you're such a klutz.

236
00:13:03,580 --> 00:13:05,320
Did you throw it too hard?

237
00:13:05,340 --> 00:13:06,560
I threw it too hard.

238
00:13:07,660 --> 00:13:08,660
Give me your hand.

239
00:13:09,490 --> 00:13:10,160
Okay.

240
00:13:10,190 --> 00:13:10,770
Here I go.

241
00:13:10,800 --> 00:13:14,830
Hey, it hurts! It hurts so much! It hurts!

242
00:13:14,850 --> 00:13:16,450
It hurts! It hurts!

243
00:13:16,480 --> 00:13:17,200
-Where does it hurt?
-It hurts!

244
00:13:17,200 --> 00:13:17,880
It hurts! It hurts!

245
00:13:17,880 --> 00:13:20,560
I hope you get a strike.

246
00:13:22,700 --> 00:13:25,440
It took me long enough
to get out with girls.

247
00:13:25,740 --> 00:13:27,540
I should just enjoy it my own way.

248
00:13:29,140 --> 00:13:31,520
Hey, let's go take purikura.

249
00:13:31,540 --> 00:13:32,980
Yeah.

250
00:13:34,030 --> 00:13:36,230
If it's okay, should we go take some too?

251
00:13:36,430 --> 00:13:37,510
Ah, let's do it.

252
00:13:37,530 --> 00:13:38,200
Yeah.

253
00:13:40,970 --> 00:13:42,380
Ta-da.

254
00:13:44,240 --> 00:13:46,380
-They turned out so well.
-Aren't we a bit too close?

255
00:13:46,380 --> 00:13:49,710
I will definitely treasure them.
Thank you, Issei.

256
00:13:49,730 --> 00:13:51,160
You're exaggerating.

257
00:13:52,360 --> 00:13:53,360
Just as I thought.

258
00:13:53,940 --> 00:13:55,650
I still care about him.

259
00:14:00,230 --> 00:14:02,690
Ren, Nanami,
let's see the ones you took too.

260
00:14:04,590 --> 00:14:05,880
Ah, sorry.

261
00:14:06,880 --> 00:14:07,480
This is it.

262
00:14:07,760 --> 00:14:11,700
[printcute]

263
00:14:20,890 --> 00:14:21,360
Eh?

264
00:14:25,780 --> 00:14:26,720
How is it?

265
00:14:41,150 --> 00:14:42,730
You look like a great match.

266
00:14:42,750 --> 00:14:44,820
Ren and Nanami both look great.

267
00:14:44,840 --> 00:14:46,770
-Heh heh.
-Really?

268
00:14:46,790 --> 00:14:48,620
Really.

269
00:14:48,970 --> 00:14:50,460
I'm a little jealous.

270
00:14:56,520 --> 00:14:57,520
What is this?

271
00:14:59,290 --> 00:15:00,690
He is doing it on purpose.

272
00:15:22,320 --> 00:15:25,120
What the heck?
I panicked over such a little thing.

273
00:15:25,160 --> 00:15:27,830
Calm down, me.

274
00:15:30,310 --> 00:15:33,040
-Sorry, I think something's on your head.
-Yeah.

275
00:15:34,370 --> 00:15:35,390
Thank you.

276
00:15:38,110 --> 00:15:39,480
Hey, Issei.

277
00:15:39,510 --> 00:15:40,730
Do you want to play the claw machine?

278
00:15:40,730 --> 00:15:42,610
Yeah, which one?

279
00:15:42,630 --> 00:15:43,470
This way.

280
00:15:51,530 --> 00:15:54,650
What's going on? How does this work?

281
00:15:54,670 --> 00:15:55,910
Let me have a try.

282
00:15:56,990 --> 00:15:58,110
Ah.

283
00:16:03,290 --> 00:16:05,840
-Well, ah, what a pity!
-What a pity!

284
00:16:05,870 --> 00:16:06,660
Let's try again.

285
00:16:06,660 --> 00:16:07,930
Yeah.

286
00:16:12,670 --> 00:16:14,730
I'm so glad you guys could come today.

287
00:16:15,140 --> 00:16:15,720
Eh.

288
00:16:16,010 --> 00:16:18,350
Because Kanako has always liked Issei.

289
00:16:19,960 --> 00:16:21,190
Ah, I see.

290
00:16:25,410 --> 00:16:28,980
-Eh?
-Haha, it's not that surprising.

291
00:16:29,450 --> 00:16:30,190
Ah.

292
00:16:30,750 --> 00:16:32,910
As her boyfriend, are you jealous?

293
00:16:34,740 --> 00:16:35,800
Sorry about that.

294
00:16:41,770 --> 00:16:44,000
Alright!

295
00:16:44,020 --> 00:16:46,550
Let's go play something too!
What do you want to play?

296
00:16:46,550 --> 00:16:48,190
-Eh, is it okay?
-Of course.

297
00:16:48,420 --> 00:16:50,870
I do have something I want to play.

298
00:16:50,900 --> 00:16:52,270
Oh, which one?

299
00:16:54,060 --> 00:16:54,690
Is it this one?

300
00:16:54,690 --> 00:16:55,840
Yeah, this is it.

301
00:16:55,870 --> 00:16:57,940
Okay.

302
00:17:01,240 --> 00:17:03,180
Ah, I'll go get some change.

303
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:05,160
Ah, I have some here.

304
00:17:05,190 --> 00:17:06,050
No way.

305
00:17:06,079 --> 00:17:07,859
I can't let a girl pay.

306
00:17:07,880 --> 00:17:09,160
Just a moment.

307
00:17:09,190 --> 00:17:10,530
Yeah.

308
00:17:14,589 --> 00:17:17,940
Ah, wait for me!

309
00:17:19,569 --> 00:17:20,730
Ren.

310
00:17:25,069 --> 00:17:26,190
Ren.

311
00:17:30,630 --> 00:17:31,410
Ren.

312
00:17:32,130 --> 00:17:33,280
At that time,

313
00:17:34,160 --> 00:17:36,290
I just touched him gently.

314
00:17:38,010 --> 00:17:40,570
His usually calm expression,

315
00:17:43,190 --> 00:17:44,460
breathing,

316
00:17:44,490 --> 00:17:46,370
and voice all became unsettled.

317
00:17:48,260 --> 00:17:50,920
It made me feel that this boy
who is better than me

318
00:17:50,930 --> 00:17:53,250
actually fell for me.

319
00:17:54,600 --> 00:17:56,580
It also gave me a sense of superiority.

320
00:17:56,580 --> 00:17:58,850
That feeling was simply amazing.

321
00:17:59,550 --> 00:18:00,640
But,

322
00:18:00,670 --> 00:18:02,910
it was all my wishful thinking,

323
00:18:02,930 --> 00:18:04,850
nothing more.

324
00:18:06,300 --> 00:18:07,450
That's right.

325
00:18:08,080 --> 00:18:09,790
A boy of such a high level

326
00:18:09,820 --> 00:18:13,180
can get any girl he wants.
How could he fall for me?

327
00:18:15,190 --> 00:18:17,880
[Coin changer]

328
00:18:15,800 --> 00:18:18,100
I'm such an idiot.

329
00:18:22,180 --> 00:18:23,250
[Coin changer]

330
00:18:26,690 --> 00:18:28,930
Oh no.

331
00:18:30,020 --> 00:18:32,950
I haven't slept much lately.

332
00:18:36,870 --> 00:18:37,800
What's going on?

333
00:18:47,770 --> 00:18:48,570
Ren!

334
00:18:48,590 --> 00:18:49,380
Ren!

335
00:18:49,400 --> 00:18:50,160
Ren!

336
00:18:50,190 --> 00:18:50,830
Ren!

337
00:18:50,850 --> 00:18:51,650
Are you okay?

338
00:18:51,670 --> 00:18:52,540
Are you okay?

339
00:18:52,570 --> 00:18:53,400
-Ren!
-Ren!

340
00:18:53,420 --> 00:18:54,510
Ren!

341
00:19:00,100 --> 00:19:01,880
So noisy.

342
00:19:01,900 --> 00:19:02,830
Ren!

343
00:19:02,860 --> 00:19:04,580
Are you okay?

344
00:19:04,610 --> 00:19:06,730
Ren!

345
00:19:08,030 --> 00:19:09,750
-Ren!
-Wake up.

346
00:19:09,770 --> 00:19:12,010
-Ren!
-Ren!

347
00:19:35,560 --> 00:19:36,440
Ah.

348
00:19:37,890 --> 00:19:39,110
Where is this?

349
00:19:43,600 --> 00:19:44,460
By the way, I...

350
00:19:44,880 --> 00:19:45,860
fell asleep.

351
00:19:48,910 --> 00:19:49,950
I remember

352
00:19:51,670 --> 00:19:53,530
when I was playing with everyone,

353
00:19:54,170 --> 00:19:56,400
I seemed to have fainted.

354
00:19:59,360 --> 00:20:00,650
Could it be

355
00:20:02,280 --> 00:20:04,610
that I hit a vital spot when I fell
and died?

356
00:20:10,180 --> 00:20:11,140
If so,

357
00:20:13,340 --> 00:20:15,680
this is heaven.

358
00:20:16,910 --> 00:20:19,470
Well, it's just that

359
00:20:19,500 --> 00:20:21,710
it feels a bit too real here.

360
00:20:25,930 --> 00:20:26,730
You're awake.

361
00:20:28,790 --> 00:20:30,940
Ah, why are you here?

362
00:20:37,030 --> 00:20:38,300
Because this

363
00:20:38,320 --> 00:20:39,840
is my house.

364
00:20:42,240 --> 00:20:44,030
Eh, then this...

365
00:20:45,530 --> 00:20:46,350
Yes,

366
00:20:48,060 --> 00:20:49,230
it's my bed.

367
00:20:51,580 --> 00:20:52,440
How could it be?

368
00:20:53,300 --> 00:20:54,210
Ah,

369
00:20:54,590 --> 00:20:56,380
did we sleep together?

370
00:21:03,710 --> 00:21:09,330
♪ Countless moments,
added up again and again ♪

371
00:21:09,350 --> 00:21:15,380
♪ To create this ordinary miracle
we hold dear ♪

372
00:21:15,440 --> 00:21:21,420
♪ Along the winding paths to freedom ♪

373
00:21:21,690 --> 00:21:26,180
♪ Each of us has been given ♪

374
00:21:26,200 --> 00:21:29,180
♪ Right here, right now,
so real and true ♪

375
00:21:29,200 --> 00:21:33,530
♪ The pieces in our hands ♪

376
00:21:33,580 --> 00:21:39,120
♪ Fitting them together, piece by piece ♪

377
00:21:39,250 --> 00:21:45,190
♪ At last, they form a perfect whole ♪

378
00:21:45,220 --> 00:21:48,270
♪ All the pain ♪

379
00:21:48,300 --> 00:21:51,080
♪ All the worries ♪

380
00:21:51,110 --> 00:21:57,350
♪ Are waiting for the day
we walk hand in hand ♪

381
00:21:57,370 --> 00:22:02,560
♪ Waiting for that day ♪

382
00:22:03,130 --> 00:22:06,160
♪ Bit by bit ♪

383
00:22:06,180 --> 00:22:09,080
♪ We put them together ♪

384
00:22:09,110 --> 00:22:12,290
♪ Until at last ♪

385
00:22:12,310 --> 00:22:15,280
♪ They form a perfect whole ♪

386
00:22:15,300 --> 00:22:18,210
♪ All the pain ♪

387
00:22:18,230 --> 00:22:21,000
♪ All the worries ♪

388
00:22:21,020 --> 00:22:27,400
♪ Are waiting for the day
we walk hand in hand ♪

389
00:22:27,430 --> 00:22:30,740
♪ Quietly waiting ♪

390
00:22:30,770 --> 00:22:33,440
♪ For the day we walk hand in hand ♪

391
00:22:33,490 --> 00:22:36,850
♪ Thoughts fill the page,
along with all that nonsense ♪

392
00:22:33,540 --> 00:22:36,230
What am I doing in someone else's house?

393
00:22:33,660 --> 00:22:36,870
[Coming Up Next]

394
00:22:36,260 --> 00:22:37,770
I changed your clothes for you.

395
00:22:36,880 --> 00:22:40,640
♪ Just one step away from you ♪

396
00:22:37,800 --> 00:22:38,760
Was it you?

397
00:22:38,800 --> 00:22:41,210
My chastity is safe!

398
00:22:38,850 --> 00:22:42,870
[My chastity is safe]

399
00:22:40,670 --> 00:22:42,560
♪ Just a gentle leap ♪

400
00:22:41,760 --> 00:22:42,760
What's wrong?

401
00:22:42,580 --> 00:22:44,640
♪ Before summer ends ♪

402
00:22:42,790 --> 00:22:45,810
Doesn't staying overnight mean
that is going to happen?

403
00:22:44,700 --> 00:22:47,770
♪ I want to leave a mark in your heart ♪

404
00:22:45,840 --> 00:22:47,710
As long as you ask me to go with you,
I will.

405
00:22:47,710 --> 00:22:49,760
Isn't this just like a doll
girls play with?

406
00:22:47,890 --> 00:22:54,700
♪ A gentle breeze blows,
and in this moment, I pray to the gods ♪

407
00:22:50,150 --> 00:22:51,150
Yeah.

408
00:22:51,380 --> 00:22:52,710
What are you going to do?

409
00:22:52,930 --> 00:22:54,280
Cheers!

410
00:22:54,280 --> 00:22:55,640
He could hook as many girls
as he wanted with ease.

411
00:22:54,720 --> 00:22:57,790
♪ OK, tomorrow's matters ♪

412
00:22:55,670 --> 00:22:57,720
Is the other person a boy or a girl?

413
00:22:57,750 --> 00:22:59,730
You like me, right?

414
00:22:57,810 --> 00:23:03,350
♪ Leave them to tomorrow's wind ♪

415
00:22:58,190 --> 00:23:03,520
[This drama is entirely fictional]

416
00:22:59,750 --> 00:23:01,060
If not,

417
00:23:01,470 --> 00:23:03,060
